# Hypothesis from wiki

When the user asks to propose, refine, or record a research hypothesis (e.g. “Propose hypotheses for dense-stand segmentation”), run **Operation: Hypothesis** from `AGENTS.md`. Detail: [[project/hypothesis-validation-loop]].

North star: [[project/research-tree-detection-ensemble]]. Production baseline: [[project/pipeline-overview]].

## Checklist

1. Read `conifervision/index.md`, `project/research-tree-detection-ensemble.md`, `project/hypothesis-validation-loop.md`, plus relevant `methods/`, `concepts/`, `sources/`.
2. Propose **2–3** candidate hypotheses in chat, each with wiki citations (`[[…]]`) and a one-line kill criterion.
3. Wait for the human to pick one (unless they already named a single hypothesis).
4. Create or update `conifervision/experiments/exp-NNN-<slug>.md` from `.templates/experiment.md` — full sections: Hypothesis, Motivation, Pseudocode, Evaluation, Success/Kill, Setup, Runs, Results placeholders, Conclusion stub, Handoff.
5. Add bullet to `conifervision/experiments/index.md`.
6. Optionally draft ADR in `project/decisions.md` (`approved to run` | `rejected`).
7. Prepend `conifervision/log.md`: `## [YYYY-MM-DD] hypothesis | …`
8. After results return: fill Results + Conclusion (`accept` | `reject` | `iterate`); refresh **Replication notes** on touched methods; flag contradictions.

Vault prose and frontmatter: **English only**. Chat with the user may be Polish.

## Forbidden

- Invent numeric thresholds not in literature; use `TBD` or “per field calibration”
- Store weights, datasets, secrets, or Delta Lake paths in this repo
- Invent production code file paths (`code-repo-integration` still TODO)
- Mass-convert `[[wikilinks]]` to OKF markdown links unless asked
- Commit without explicit user request
- Claim to “prove” a hypothesis — use validate / reject / iterate
- Skip human gate before implying a GPU/training run is approved

## Experiment frontmatter (minimum)

`type: Experiment`, `title`, `description`, `status: draft|stable|deprecated`, `hypothesis`, `area`, `metrics`, `related_methods`, `sources`, `generated.by` / `generated.at`.
